@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

title Thirty-day uptime evidence pipeline

rectangle "Hard semantic authorities" #D1C4E9 {
  component "Rocq\nalgebra and refinement" as Rocq #B39DDB
  component "TLA+ / Apalache\nconcurrent protocol" as TLA #9575CD
  component "Loom / Rust\nownership and code" as Loom #7E57C2
}

rectangle "Quantitative reliability" #BBDEFB {
  component "Storm\n30-day CTMC queries" as Storm #64B5F6
  component "Storm-pars\nexact parameter functions" as Pars #42A5F5
  component "mCRL2\ndeadlock + overlap" as MCRL #2196F3
}

rectangle "Calibration and exploration" #C8E6C9 {
  component "historical backtest + fault injection\ncurrent 60h calibration" as Measure #81C784
  component "Wolfram (opt-in)\nrobust feasible region" as Wolfram #66BB6A
}

rectangle "Evidence result" #FFF9C4 {
  component "720-hour engineering envelope\nparameters + provenance" as Projection #FFF176
  component "calibrated release projection\nfail closed" as Release #FFD54F
}

Rocq --> Storm : certified service interface
TLA --> Storm : progress and fault premises
Loom --> Storm : bounded ownership premises
MCRL --> Projection : parallelism retained
Measure --> Storm : calibrated rates and buckets
Storm --> Pars : reduced parametric controls
Storm --> Projection : exact / sound query results
Pars --> Projection : rational boundaries
Projection --> Wolfram : machine-readable report
Wolfram --> Storm : candidate thresholds rechecked
Projection --> Release
Measure --> Release
Rocq --> Release
TLA --> Release
Loom --> Release

note bottom of Release #FFCDD2
No probability overrides a failed hard invariant.
No missing or stale calibration produces a release projection.
end note
@enduml
